Update the contents and commit message per new style info in CLAUDE.md.

This is good and covers a lot of good information, but it doesn't
clearly illustrate the workflow and cycle that's intended to take place
with this.

Essentially this implements an agentic loop with a human
collaborator. The whole purpose of this system is to go from a human
idea to working code, using LLM to assist with it.

The guide does need a clear-cut example of the sequence of commands that
will be run. Currently a human operator still runs commands to trigger
the LLM / contributor behavior.

There should be a brief end-to-end example of prompting via email,
processing it, providing feedback, and ultimately applying patches.
